#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:3
msgid "Developing Extensions"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:5
msgid ""
"Zed extensions are Git repositories containing an `extension.toml` manifest. "
"They can provide languages, themes, debuggers, snippets, and MCP servers."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:7
msgid "Extension Features"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:9
msgid "Extensions can provide:"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:11
msgid "[Languages](./languages.md)"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:12
msgid "[Debuggers](./debugger-extensions.md)"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:13
msgid "[Themes](./themes.md)"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:14
msgid "[Icon Themes](./icon-themes.md)"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:15
msgid "[Snippets](./snippets.md)"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:16
msgid "[MCP Servers](./mcp-extensions.md)"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:18
msgid "Developing an Extension Locally"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:20
msgid ""
"Before starting to develop an extension for Zed, be sure to [install Rust "
"via rustup](https://www.rust-lang.org/tools/install)."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:22
msgid ""
"Rust must be installed via rustup. If you have Rust installed via homebrew "
"or otherwise, installing dev extensions will not work."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:24
msgid ""
"When developing an extension, you can use it in Zed without needing to "
"publish it by installing it as a _dev extension_."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:26
msgid ""
"From the extensions page, click the `Install Dev Extension` button (or the "
"<code class=\"hljs\">zed: install dev extension</code> action) and select "
"the directory containing your extension."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:28
msgid ""
"If you need to troubleshoot, check Zed.log (<code class=\"hljs\">zed: open "
"log</code>) for additional output. For debug output, close and relaunch Zed "
"from the command line with `zed --foreground`, which shows more verbose INFO-"
"level logs."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:30
msgid ""
"If you already have the published version of the extension installed, the "
"published version will be uninstalled prior to the installation of the dev "
"extension. After successful installation, the `Extensions` page will "
"indicate that the upstream extension is \"Overridden by dev extension\"."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:32
msgid "Directory Structure of a Zed Extension"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:34
msgid ""
"A Zed extension is a Git repository that contains an `extension.toml`. This "
"file must contain some basic information about the extension:"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:37
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"id = \"my-extension\"\n"
"name = \"My extension\"\n"
"version = \"0.0.1\"\n"
"schema_version = 1\n"
"authors = [\"Your Name <you@example.com>\"]\n"
"description = \"Example extension\"\n"
"repository = \"https://github.com/your-name/my-zed-extension\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:47
msgid ""
"In addition to this, there are several other optional files and directories "
"that can be used to add functionality to a Zed extension. An example "
"directory structure of an extension that provides all capabilities is as "
"follows:"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:66
msgid "WebAssembly"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:68
msgid ""
"Procedural parts of extensions are written in Rust and compiled to "
"WebAssembly. To develop an extension that includes custom code, include a "
"`Cargo.toml` like this:"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:70
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[package]\n"
"name = \"my-extension\"\n"
"version = \"0.0.1\"\n"
"edition = \"2021\"\n"
"\n"
"[lib]\n"
"crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]\n"
"\n"
"[dependencies]\n"
"zed_extension_api = \"0.1.0\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:83
msgid ""
"Use the latest version of the [`zed_extension_api`](https://crates.io/crates/"
"zed_extension_api) available on crates.io. Make sure it's still [compatible "
"with Zed versions](https://github.com/zed-industries/zed/blob/main/crates/"
"extension_api#compatible-zed-versions) you want to support."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:85
msgid ""
"In the `src/lib.rs` file in your Rust crate you will need to define a struct "
"for your extension and implement the `Extension` trait, as well as use the "
"`register_extension!` macro to register your extension:"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:91
msgid "// ... state\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:95
msgid "// ...\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:101
msgid ""
"`stdout`/`stderr` is forwarded directly to the Zed process. In order to see "
"`println!`/`dbg!` output from your extension, you can start Zed in your "
"terminal with a `--foreground` flag."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:103
msgid "Forking and cloning the repo"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:105
msgid "Fork the repo"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:107
msgid ""
"**Note:** It is very helpful if you fork the `zed-industries/extensions` "
"repo to a personal GitHub account instead of a GitHub organization, as this "
"allows Zed staff to push any needed changes to your PR to expedite the "
"publishing process."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:109
msgid "Clone the repo to your local machine"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:112
msgid ""
"# Substitute the url of your fork here:\n"
"# git clone https://github.com/zed-industries/extensions\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:119
msgid "Extension License Requirements"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:121
msgid ""
"As of October 1st, 2025, extension repositories must include a license. The "
"following licenses are accepted:"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:124
msgid "[Apache 2.0](https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0)"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:125
msgid "[BSD 2-Clause](https://opensource.org/license/bsd-2-clause)"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:126
msgid "[BSD 3-Clause](https://opensource.org/license/bsd-3-clause)"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:127
msgid "[CC BY 4.0](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0)"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:128
msgid "[GNU GPLv3](https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-3.0.en.html)"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:129
msgid "[GNU LGPLv3](https://www.gnu.org/licenses/lgpl-3.0.en.html)"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:130
msgid "[MIT](https://opensource.org/license/mit)"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:131
msgid "[Unlicense](https://unlicense.org)"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:132
msgid "[zlib](https://opensource.org/license/zlib)"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:134
msgid ""
"This allows us to distribute the resulting binary produced from your "
"extension code to our users. Without a valid license, the pull request to "
"add or update your extension in the following steps will fail CI."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:137
msgid ""
"Your license file should be at the root of your extension repository. Any "
"filename that has `LICENCE` or `LICENSE` as a prefix (case insensitive) will "
"be inspected to ensure it matches one of the accepted licenses. See the "
"[license validation source code](https://github.com/zed-industries/"
"extensions/blob/main/src/lib/license.js)."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:139
msgid ""
"This license requirement applies only to your extension code itself (the "
"code that gets compiled into the extension binary). It does not apply to any "
"tools your extension may download or interact with, such as language servers "
"or other external dependencies. If your repository contains both extension "
"code and other projects (like a language server), you are not required to "
"relicense those other projects — only the extension code needs to be one of "
"the aforementioned accepted licenses."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:143
msgid "Extension Publishing Prerequisites"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:145
msgid ""
"Before publishing your extension, make sure that you have chosen a unique "
"extension ID for your extension in the [extension manifest](#directory-"
"structure-of-a-zed-extension). This will be the primary identifier for your "
"extension and cannot be changed after your extension has been published. "
"Also, ensure that you have filled out all the required fields in the "
"manifest."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:149
msgid ""
"Furthermore, please make sure that your extension fulfills the following "
"preconditions before you move on to publishing your extension:"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:151
msgid ""
"Extension IDs and names must not contain the words `zed`, `Zed` or "
"`extension`, since they are all Zed extensions."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:152
msgid ""
"Your extension ID should provide some information on what your extension "
"tries to accomplish. E.g. for themes, it should be suffixed with `-theme`, "
"snippet extensions should be suffixed with `-snippets` and so on. An "
"exception to that rule are extension that provide support for languages or "
"popular tooling that people would expect to find under that ID. You can take "
"a look at the list of [existing extensions](https://github.com/zed-"
"industries/extensions/blob/main/extensions.toml) to get a grasp on how this "
"usually is enforced."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:153
msgid ""
"Extensions should provide something that is not yet available in the "
"marketplace as opposed to fixing something that could be resolved within an "
"existing extension. For example, if you find that an existing extension's "
"support for a language server is not functioning properly, first try "
"contributing a fix to the existing extension as opposed to submitting a new "
"extension immediately."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:154
msgid ""
"If you receive no response or reaction within the upstream repository within "
"a reasonable amount of time, feel free to submit a pull request that aims to "
"fix said issue. Please ensure that you provide your previous efforts within "
"the pull request to the extensions repository for adding your extension. Zed "
"maintainers will then decide on how to proceed on a case by case basis."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:155
msgid ""
"Extensions that intend to provide a language, debugger or MCP server must "
"not ship the language server as part of the extension. Instead, the "
"extension should either download the language server or check for the "
"availability of the language server in the users environment using the APIs "
"as provided by the [Zed Rust Extension API](https://docs.rs/"
"zed_extension_api/latest/zed_extension_api/)."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:156
msgid ""
"Themes and icon themes should not be published as part of extensions that "
"provide other features, e.g. language support. Instead, they should be "
"published as a distinct extension. This also applies to theme and icon "
"themes living in the same repository."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:158
msgid ""
"Note that non-compliance will be raised during the publishing process by "
"reviewers and delay the release of your extension."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:160
msgid "Publishing your extension"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:162
msgid ""
"To publish an extension, open a PR to [the `zed-industries/extensions` repo]"
"(https://github.com/zed-industries/extensions)."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:164
msgid "In your PR, do the following:"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:166
msgid ""
"Add your extension as a Git submodule within the `extensions/` directory "
"under the `extensions/{extension-id}` path"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:173
msgid ""
"All extension submodules must use HTTPS URLs and not SSH URLS (`git@github."
"com`)."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:175
msgid ""
"Add a new entry to the top-level `extensions.toml` file containing your "
"extension:"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:177
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[my-extension]\n"
"submodule = \"extensions/my-extension\"\n"
"version = \"0.0.1\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:183
msgid ""
"If your extension is in a subdirectory within the submodule, you can use the "
"`path` field to point to where the extension resides:"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:185
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[my-extension]\n"
"submodule = \"extensions-my-extension\"\n"
"path = \"packages/zed\"\n"
"version = \"0.0.1\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:192
msgid ""
"Note that the [required extension license](#extension-license-requirements) "
"must reside at the specified path, a license at the root of the repository "
"will not work. However, you are free to symlink an existing license within "
"the repository or choose an alternative license from the list of accepted "
"licenses for the extension code."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:194
msgid ""
"Run `pnpm sort-extensions` to ensure `extensions.toml` and `.gitmodules` are "
"sorted"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:196
msgid ""
"Once your PR is merged, the extension will be packaged and published to the "
"Zed extension registry."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:198
msgid "Updating an extension"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:200
msgid ""
"To update an extension, open a PR to [the `zed-industries/extensions` repo]"
"(https://github.com/zed-industries/extensions)."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:202
msgid "In your PR do the following:"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:204
msgid ""
"Update the extension's submodule to the commit of the new version. For this, "
"you can run"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:207
msgid "# From the root of the repository:\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:211
msgid ""
"to update your extension to the latest commit available in your remote "
"repository."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:213
msgid "Update the `version` field for the extension in `extensions.toml`"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:214
msgid ""
"Make sure the `version` matches the one set in `extension.toml` at the "
"particular commit."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:216
msgid ""
"If you'd like to automate this process, there is a [community GitHub Action]"
"(https://github.com/huacnlee/zed-extension-action) you can use."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/developing-extensions.md:218
msgid ""
"**Note:** If your extension repository has a different license, you'll need "
"to update it to be one of the [accepted extension licenses](#extension-"
"license-requirements) before publishing your update."
msgstr ""
